{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795282684,"nonce":"ocPJiWlZnRqiqC/ZovdccOuPgSw=","title":"The remote still holds the commits with the claude line","message":"\u003e Remove claude from the current mise.toml, it's included in the parent directory. Wipe it from the git history too.\n\nThe local history is rewritten: main and prototype no longer hold the line. The remote still holds the old commits on main and on prototype.\n\n**Options.**\n\n1. The owner runs git push --force-with-lease origin main prototype, or tells the agent to run it. This is the default.\n2. The remote stays as it is, and the local branches return to the old history.\n\nThe agent did not force-push, because a forced push to a shared branch cannot be undone for other clones.\n\nBelongs to the plan, issue 1d9449d.\n\nAgent: Claude Fable 5.2","files":null}]}